the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base annuity_deposit includes these resources:
    temporal.

the functions are:
    the effective date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the gross amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the account value of the policy before *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the premium tax of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the bonus rate of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the bonus of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the net deposit of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the new account value of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the premium tax rate of the plan is *a number*.
    the account value of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.

the templates are:
    *an activity* is a deposit.
    *an activity* fails the check *a code*.

the knowledge base annuity_deposit includes:

the text of "Deposit/Transaction.xml" is at "sources/Deposit/Transaction.xml".

the premium tax rate of the plan is 0.0235, as stated in "PlanFields.csv" at PremiumTaxRate.

% An activity of this program is a deposit: the Deposit transaction it processes.
an activity is a deposit if
    the effective date of the activity is a date.

rule premium_tax with provenance "Deposit/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable PremiumTaxMV:
the premium tax of an activity is an amount N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the premium tax rate of the plan is a number K
    and N = round(M * K * 100) / 100.

rule bonus_rate with provenance "Deposit/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable BonusRateMV:
the bonus rate of an activity is a number N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and M >= 100000
    and N = 0.02
    otherwise the activity is a deposit
    and N = 0.01.

rule bonus with provenance "Deposit/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable BonusMV:
the bonus of an activity is an amount N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the premium tax of the activity is an amount K
    and the bonus rate of the activity is a number P
    and N = round((M - K) * P * 100) / 100.

rule net_deposit with provenance "Deposit/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable NetDepositMV:
the net deposit of an activity is an amount N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the premium tax of the activity is an amount K
    and the bonus of the activity is an amount P
    and N = round((M - K + P) * 100) / 100.

rule new_account_value with provenance "Deposit/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable NewAccountValueMV:
the new account value of an activity is an amount N if
    the account value of the policy before the activity is an amount M
    and the net deposit of the activity is an amount K
    and N = round((M + K) * 100) / 100.

% The deposit must be a positive amount.
rule d001 with provenance "Deposit/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression D001:
an activity fails the check "D001" if
    the gross amount of the activity <= 0.

% Deposits above $1,000,000 need home office approval.
rule d002 with provenance "Deposit/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression D002:
an activity fails the check "D002" if
    the gross amount of the activity > 1000000.

rule copy_account_value with provenance "Deposit/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field AccountValue:
the account value of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the new account value of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

scenario steady_saver_d1 is:
    the effective date of d1 is 2020-03-15.
    the gross amount of d1 is 50000.
    the account value of the policy before d1 is 0.
    net_deposit expects answers ["the net deposit of d1 is 49313.25"].
    new_account_value expects answers ["the new account value of d1 is 49313.25"].
    checks expects answers [].
    policy_after_account_value expects answers ["the account value of the policy after d1 is 49313.25"].

